WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.222
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.222 --> 00:00:14.021
Today, scripts: a few lines of code on a trigger that can do the work of ten.

5
00:00:15.433 --> 00:00:20.308
Open Mechanics, then Advanced, then Triggers, and scroll down to show nights.

6
00:00:20.308 --> 00:00:26.196
It's recurring, and its whole job is to count every show the player puts on, all season long.

7
00:00:26.633 --> 00:00:27.633
Two conditions.

8
00:00:27.633 --> 00:00:33.442
First a quick word match on the player's action, for things like perform, juggle or throw.

9
00:00:33.442 --> 00:00:39.121
Only if that matches does the AI check run: is the player really performing for a crowd?

10
00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:40.652
Then the script.

11
00:00:40.652 --> 00:00:44.520
It runs after the conditions pass and before the effects.

12
00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:49.609
It adds one to a counter in storage, and storage is kept from turn to turn.

13
00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:55.616
Its effects list is empty, because the script adds the effects itself.

14
00:00:57.033 --> 00:01:02.766
On the third show it pushes two effects: word's got round, and Dreamer likes you ten points more.

15
00:01:02.766 --> 00:01:05.426
On the tenth, the act's name goes on a wagon.

16
00:01:05.426 --> 00:01:08.794
Every other show it sets skip, so nothing happens at all.

17
00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:13.079
Scripts can also read the world with check,

18
00:01:13.079 --> 00:01:18.635
using the same types as conditions: where the party is, the turn, resources, flags.

19
00:01:18.635 --> 00:01:23.656
Mix that with storage and one script can replace a whole stack of triggers.

20
00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:30.667
Two limits. Every script in a phase shares half a second, and past that the rest get skipped.

21
00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:33.799
And it runs boxed in, with no require and no timers.

22
00:01:33.799 --> 00:01:38.256
I tested this one on my own machine before it went in, and you should too.

23
00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:40.818
That's scripts.

24
00:01:40.818 --> 00:01:43.428
Ours is linked in the description.

25
00:01:43.428 --> 00:01:47.573
Next time, we put triggers to work: music on anything.

26
00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:51.981
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

